#!/bin/sh
# In the container (tools/browser/run): build, then an XFCE desktop on Xvfb with a few icons on it and
# the wall over it, shared by x11vnc and served by websockify with a page of our own (index.html).
#
#   serve WxH [RETRO-WALL OPTION]...
set -eu
size=$1
shift
cargo build --release --locked
Xvfb :1 -screen 0 "${size}x24" -nolisten tcp +extension GLX -noreset >/dev/null 2>&1 &
export DISPLAY=:1 XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP=XFCE
while ! [ -e /tmp/.X11-unix/X1 ]; do sleep 0.1; done
eval "$(dbus-launch --sh-syntax)"
# something on the desktop to click
mkdir -p ~/Desktop/Projects
echo "Double-click me: I open in Mousepad." >~/Desktop/notes.txt
xfwm4 --compositor=off >/dev/null 2>&1 &
xfdesktop >/dev/null 2>&1 &
x11vnc -display :1 -forever -shared -nopw -localhost -quiet -rfbport 5900 >/dev/null 2>&1 &
cp /src/tools/browser/index.html /usr/share/novnc/index.html
websockify --web /usr/share/novnc 6080 localhost:5900 >/dev/null 2>&1 &
sleep 2 # xfdesktop up, so the wall hands it the picture
# software GL on every core would starve the server and the viewer: the wall yields to them
LP_NUM_THREADS=4 nice -n 10 /target/release/retro-wall --software "$@"
